   <!--
   =====================================================================
   TENNESSEE (TN) - NO STATE INCOME TAX TEST CASE
   =====================================================================

   Tennessee has NO state income tax on any type of income as of 2021:
   - W-2 wages: NOT TAXED
   - Investment income: NOT TAXED (Hall Tax repealed in 2021)
   - Self-employment income: NOT TAXED
   - All other income types: NOT TAXED

   Historical Note - Hall Income Tax (REPEALED):
   Tennessee previously had a "Hall Tax" on interest and dividends:
   - Tax rate: 6% on interest and dividends only
   - Exemptions existed for low-income taxpayers
   - Fully REPEALED effective January 1, 2021

   Tennessee is now one of 9 states with no personal income tax.

   This test case validates (2025):
   - W-2 wages ($95,000) are NOT taxed
   - Interest income ($3,000) is NOT taxed (Hall Tax repealed)
   - Dividend income ($7,000) is NOT taxed (Hall Tax repealed)
   - State tax = $0 for all income types

   Income breakdown:
   - W-2 wages: $95,000
   - Interest income: $3,000
   - Qualified dividends: $7,000
   - Total income: $105,000

   Expected Results:
   - Federal AGI: $105,000
   - Federal Taxable: ~$75,000 (after standard deduction, MFJ)
   - Federal Tax: ~$10,500 (approximate, with preferential dividend rate)
   - TN State Tax: $0 (no income tax since 2021)
   =====================================================================
   -->

